WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.320
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:08.220
Come!  The new card created from my will!

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.020
Master Storm Access!

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.090
No way...

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.000
Link Summon!

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.870
Appear, Link 5!

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:25.540
Chimera Hydradrive Dragrid!

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.250
Neuron Link?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.860
It's the ultimate system I created.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.310
I pull out and use the 
human brains' capabilities.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.990
That's how you built that Data Storm?

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.490
I activate my Skill!

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.260
Another Skill?

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:55.500
Watch and feel my duel that 
surpasses your imagination!

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:18.340
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:25.130
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:32.450
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:39.020
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:45.770
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:53.000
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:59.710
I want to share your pain

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.980
What's happening?

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.010
Enough already!

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.940
Let me log out!

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.150
This is a nightmare.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.150
If Bohman is telling the truth...

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:58.640
...the Neuron Link will keep sacrificing 
people logged into LINK VRAINS.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.630
We must stop this immediately.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.810
Data Storm...

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:09.260
It's also using the people 
trapped inside LINK VRAINS.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.040
Come!  The new card created from my will!

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.010
Master Storm Access!

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:44.700
If nothing changes, the people in LINK 
VRAINS will increase Bohman's power.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.310
Analyze the Neuron Link immediately!

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:54.280
Tackling a system this large 
makes me tremble with excitement.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.250
Genome, this isn't for fun.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.140
I know.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:03.960
Chimera Hydradrive Dragrid's 
effect activates!

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.930
I use one Hydradrive Counter to roll a die.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.000
Judgment Dice!

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:18.170
I select a Draghead of the Attribute I roll, 
and I return Dragrid to the Extra Deck.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:22.910
I Special Summon the selected Draghead.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.910
I rolled Water Attribute.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:30.380
Appear, Chimera Hydradrive Draghead - Aqua!

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.580
Aqua?

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.970
Draghead - Aqua's effect activates!

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:55.710
It negates monsters' effects, other 
than the ones next to its links.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.730
What?

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.680
So Quantum's effects are negated?

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.680
Then it can't attack!

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.650
That was his way to turn the tables!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.620
I set one card and end my turn.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:13.330
Draghead - Aqua's effect!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:18.600
By returning it to the Extra 
Deck, I Special Summon Dragrid.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:27.770
Due to Dragrid's effect, I 
place one Hydradrive Counter.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:31.930
I knew you were going to summon Quantum.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.550
How did you know?

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:41.990
The Neuron Link allowed 
me to hear many voices.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.460
What?

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:52.460
LINK VRAINS is filled with people who 
admire, awed and want to challenge Playmaker.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:58.440
- Playmaker will...
 - With that move...
- He wins by...
- Playmaker is...

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.910
They've become a part of my thinking.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:08.380
And that's how you figured out 
that I'd summon Quantum Dragon.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:13.850
Playmaker, I'm not your only opponent.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:20.020
All the people in LINK VRAINS 
are also your enemies!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:24.500
You trapped people to use them for this?

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.230
There's only a limited number 
of people in LINK VRAINS.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.780
If you keep using them, 
you'll eventually run out-

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.580
That's not true.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.310
The number of people in 
LINK VRAINS is increasing.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:38.800
What?

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.280
What do you mean?

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:45.520
Humans are curious.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:51.900
Due to a greater system error than before, 
SOL is receiving a deluge of complaints.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:58.930
LINK VRAINS's users can't 
log out due to this error.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.260
Zaizen, big trouble!

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.140
There's a rapid increase in logins!

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.400
Log in?  What do you mean?

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:12.410
Reports have spread via internet, 
so curious people are logging in!

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.650
No way!  They won't be able to log out!

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.820
Is this for real?

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.290
What's this?  Wow!

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.540
It'd be horrible if it was real life.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:30.060
Good thing I'm an avatar.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:31.850
Such tension!

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.500
Why are they logging in?

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.940
Log out!

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:42.860
Why can't I log out?

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:45.040
It's happening again!

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.680
No more!  I want to go home to the max!

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:52.860
Bohman intentionally allowed logins.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.690
To think so many people would log in...

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:01.430
Why are there so many fools?

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.400
It's no good.  The logins keep coming.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:08.900
He's using humans' foolishness 
to his advantage!

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:20.310
Humans are logging in of their own free will!

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.280
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.150
I activate my Skill!

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.890
He's using his Skill again!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:37.220
You'll be defeated by the same 
people you're trying to save.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:53.020
Stop it!  Someone let me out!

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:54.180
Help me-

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:58.620
Created from my will!

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:01.350
Master Storm Access!

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:11.800
To have no more victims, let's defeat 
him and stop the Neuron Link!

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:12.730
Yeah!

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.970
Is he selecting people in user account order?

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:21.940
Since we're using admin 
privileges, we're safe for now.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:25.410
But our turn will come eventually.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.150
If we can shut down the system before then...

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.620
Just us two can't keep up with this amount!

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:36.590
The two LINK VRAINS overlap with each other.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.020
What's that have to do with the Neuron Link?

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:43.930
The overlap is the key 
to operating the system.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:48.530
So if we can pull them apart, 
we can stop the Neuron Link?

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:50.670
I'm guessing so.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.970
Let's look into that method.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:55.000
I already am.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:00.810
Playmaker, I thank you from my heart.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.820
We don't need thanks from you!

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.820
Besides, do you even have a heart?

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:07.650
I do.

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:13.690
Playmaker, you're the one 
who developed my heart.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.970
I'm your evolved form, so to speak.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:22.620
You can't defeat me.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:25.440
I'm willing to let you surrender.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.640
I'll place your data in a 
special place inside me.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:35.880
I promise to give you 
happiness inside me forever.

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:38.480
What happiness?

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:42.660
No Lost Incident.  No loneliness or setbacks.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:47.800
Memories you should've had, Playmaker.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:51.400
Those are fake memories you're creating!

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:54.060
I don't need them!

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:57.370
I'll fulfill the wishes of my fallen friends!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:01.340
You don't like the new world I'm creating?

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:06.080
I don't accept ideals built 
upon sacrificing others!

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.700
So you still think that humans are superior.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:13.040
That's too bad.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:18.290
You have such advanced ideas, but you're 
still trapped within humanity's limits.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:22.160
You insult the worth of your own existence.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.030
I've heard enough from you!

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:27.020
It's too bad.

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:29.530
Dragrid's effect activates!

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.000
Judgment Dice!

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.740
I rolled Flame Attribute.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:41.890
I Special Summon Chimera 
Hydradrive Draghead - Flame!

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:53.290
That punk!  Flame too?

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:55.440
This is the end.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.230
Draghead - Flame's effect activates!

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:04.400
When it's Special Summoned, it destroy 
monsters that aren't next to its links!

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:10.100
If Quantum Dragon is gone, 
Playmaker will be defeated!

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:13.880
Survive this, Playmaker!

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.610
Go, Draghead - Flame!

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.390
Cyberse Synchron's effect from the graveyard!

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:26.990
When a battle or effect will destroy 
a monster in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.230
...I can banish this card instead!

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.170
That was close!

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.810
So you avoided it.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.170
Then let's battle.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:42.410
Draghead - Flame attacks Quantum Dragon!

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:52.050
I end my turn.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:54.790
We managed to survive.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.520
Draghead - Flame's effect!

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.670
At the end of either of our turns,

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:04.240
I return this card to the Extra Deck to Special Summon Dragrid.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:11.470
Due to Dragrid's effect, I 
place one Hydradrive Counter.

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:18.610
What's up?

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:21.610
It's nothing.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:30.090
We're not making much progress.

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:35.060
It'll take a lot of time to 
affect LINK VRAINS's systems.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:42.270
He managed to survive this turn, but Bohman 
may activate his Skill again next turn.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:45.730
If so, Playmaker will be further in trouble.

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.270
Skill...

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.240
That's right!  The Skill!

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:52.900
What about the Skill?

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:55.160
It's been bugging me.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:59.950
When Bohman uses his Skill, 
he uses a lot of power.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:05.320
So can he keep LINK VRAINS 
overlapped perfectly?

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.790
Maybe there's a vulnerability.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.530
If we target that...

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:16.480
I see.  But he only uses 
his Skill for a moment.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:20.420
That's not enough time for us to overload it.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:24.320
But if we can also attack from LINK VRAINS...

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.540
From LINK VRAINS?

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.890
But we have no one there-

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:29.740
We do!

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:33.730
Zaizen and Ghost Girl?

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:37.320
But will they trust us?

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.790
There's no time to argue.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.530
We have to do it.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:47.840
Can you hear me, Ghost Girl and Zaizen?

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:51.470
Whoever's accessing knows who we are.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.740
My name is Faust.

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:54.940
Faust?

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:56.670
A Knight of Hanoi!

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:59.640
I'll keep this short.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:09.130
I hear many voices inside me.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.130
The ultimate world will soon be created.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.130
From all possibilities, I'll choose the ideal world.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.670
A world that will lead to the ideal path.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:26.040
But it won't be a fair one!

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:29.040
There's no need for that.

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:34.280
Compared to us, humans are 
individually very different.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.520
If I respect all individuals, 
the world will collapse.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.750
Leading to confrontations and fights.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.490
That's been the case 
throughout human history.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:50.230
Individual thoughts clash and create strife.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:56.440
Since I'll unite everything into a single 
ultimate thought, only I should exist.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.080
The ultimate ideal is a single existence.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:05.240
That'll bring peace and 
lead to a glorious world.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.980
You're lonely.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:11.380
I'm lonely?

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:24.630
When I was lonely, I only had 
a futile desire for revenge.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.950
But I met many friends.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:32.370
While we clashed at times, my views expanded.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:38.060
There's something you can see for the 
first time by listen to your friends.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:40.950
By accepting each other.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:46.570
By uniting everything into one, 
I'll guide the ideal path.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:50.820
I'm saying the same thing as you, Playmaker.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:55.170
No, your method will sacrifice everything!

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:58.400
And what lies ahead will be a blockade.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.770
A closed future!

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:03.370
I'll live together with the Ignis!

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:05.840
I believe in an open future!

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:11.330
Pull apart the two LINK VRAINS by straining 
it from both the inside and outside.

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.560
That's right.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:17.460
The chance arises when large amounts 
of data are created inside LINK VRAINS.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:20.820
In other words, when Bohman 
activates his Skill.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.920
Bohman's Skill...

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:25.290
I get the gist.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.760
There's no time.  That's everything.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:35.850
We're supposed to trust the Knights 
of Hanoi after they tormented us?

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:38.740
They have no reason to trick us.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:44.240
Since Revolver was defeated, 
they want revenge.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.580
Revenge...

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:51.950
I don't know when we'll fall 
prey to the Neuron Link.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.420
Decide, Akira!

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:57.890
Let's do it.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:02.620
I have just the right tool for this moment.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.740
What's that?

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:09.330
Call it a virus bomb.

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:12.300
It should be effective for this plan.

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:15.310
It's a race against time.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:18.830
Let's hope Bohman doesn't notice.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.310
Keep accessing from our side.

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:22.810
Okay.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:27.210
Bohman, I won't let you 
create your ideal world!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:29.550
I will win this duel!

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:32.290
My turn!  I draw!

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.820
I summon Clock Wyvern!

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:47.240
When it's summoned, I can halve its 
ATK to Special Summon a Clock Token!

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:50.540
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:53.780
The summoning condition 
is one Normal Monster.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.250
Link Summon!

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:59.720
Link 1 Link Spider!

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.450
Link Spider's effect activates!

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:08.430
From my hand, I Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower Normal Monster next to its link!

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:10.380
Come, Protron!

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:16.400
Appear again!  The circuit 
that leads to the future!

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:20.340
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.010
Link Summon!

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:26.200
Appear, Link 2 Clock Spartoi!

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:29.810
Clock Spartoi's effect activates!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:36.250
When it's Link Summoned, I add Cynet 
Fusion from my deck to my hand!

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:40.220
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:43.460
The summoning condition 
is one Level 1 monster!

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:46.900
Link Summon!

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:49.930
Appear, Link 1 Linkuriboh!

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:54.140
No matter how many times you Link Summon,

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:58.490
I have Chimera Hydradrive Dragrid on my field.

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:01.650
Your monsters can't stand up against it.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:05.520
Be quiet!  Don't brag just 
because you have a Link 5!

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:08.750
Clock Spartoi's effect activates!

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:13.220
When a monster is Special 
Summoned next to its link...

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:16.280
...I Special Summon a Level 4 or lower  Cyberse from

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:19.230
my graveyard by negating its effects!

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:22.230
Come, Clock Wyvern!

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:27.200
I activate the spell card, Cynet Fusion!

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:33.620
I send Fusion Materials from my 
hand and field to the graveyard...

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:36.300
...to Special Summon a Fusion Monster!

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:43.490
I fuse Clock Wyvern, Linkuriboh 
and Clock Spartoi!

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:46.490
A Fusion Summon.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:47.960
Go!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:53.000
The strong ones gather 
before its grand wings!

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.400
Become a new legend!

00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.700
Fusion Summon!

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:07.540
Come out!  Cyberse Clock Dragon!

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:18.990
We're going all out!

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.230
Ah.  Clock Dragon.

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:23.960
We're only getting started!

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:26.430
Cyberse Clock Dragon's effect!

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:33.450
When it's Fusion Summoned, for every 
Fusion Material Link Monster's Marker...

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:36.160
...I send a card from my 
deck to the graveyard!

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:41.880
And it gains 1000 ATK per card!

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:44.290
We sent three cards.

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:48.570
So Cyberse Clock Dragon gains 3000 ATK!

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:52.320
5500 ATK.

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:53.610
How's that?

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:56.240
It's now stronger than Dragrid!

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:03.630
Time for you to lose, Bohman!

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:09.490
I was told repeatedly

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:16.940
Only tales of dreams

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:23.910
Is my life precious?

00:22:24.170 --> 00:22:26.880
Make up for  Make up for

00:22:27.270 --> 00:22:34.420
The next sentimental

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:45.670
I'm not a machine

00:22:48.390 --> 00:22:52.110
I cry a single tear

00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:57.310
A single answer moves me

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:07.690
We helplessly sing for someone we can't reach

00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:13.120
Are you ready?

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:18.470
Oh oh oh

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:23.670
Are you ready?

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:30.780
Are you ready?

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:41.970
As long as he has the Neuron 
Link, there's no way to win.

00:23:41.970 --> 00:23:47.330
Playmaker is paralyzed against 
Bohman's overwhelming power.

00:23:47.330 --> 00:23:53.560
With not a moment to spare, Ai gets an idea.

00:23:53.560 --> 00:23:56.650
Which he's willing to sacrifice his life for.

00:23:56.650 --> 00:23:59.420
What are you planning to do, Ai?

00:23:59.420 --> 00:24:03.590
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Unwavering Instinct

00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:06.240
Into the VRAINS!
